0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","article",null,{"className":"pt-16 pb-16","children":[["$","$L2",null,{}],null,false,["$","div",null,{"className":"relative -mt-[10.4rem] flex items-end","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"container z-10 relative lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_48rem_1fr] text-white pb-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"col-start-1 col-span-1 md:col-start-2 md:col-span-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"uppercase text-sm mb-6","children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":["Reproduction Health",false]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"","children":["$","h1",null,{"className":"mb-6 text-3xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl","children":"Foods that Boost Fertility"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 md:gap-16","children":[false,["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm","children":"Date Published"}],["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-06-15T19:00:00.000Z","children":"06/16/2026"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-[80vh] select-none","children":["$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute pointer-events-none left-0 bottom-0 w-full h-1/2 bg-linear-to-t from-black to-transparent"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col items-center gap-4 pt-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"payload-richtext prose md:prose-md dark:prose-invert max-w-[48rem] mx-auto","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["Changing your diet can increase your fertility and can positively affect your chances of becoming pregnant. There are several foods you can add or remove from your diet that can impact your overall chances of becoming pregnant."],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","h4","1",{"children":[["$","br","0",{}],["$","strong","1",{"children":"THINGS TO EAT AND THINGS TO AVOID"}]]}],["$","p","2",{"children":[["$","br","0",{}],"We recommend reducing red meat intake, eliminating Trans fats (such as donuts, pastries and all fried foods), and ensuring that at least 50% of every meal is composed of fruits and vegetables. Use olive oil for bread, dressings and cooking. It’s high in monounsaturated fat, which may be beneficial for women undergoing IVF treatment, and is good for general health. Reducing sugar intake is always a good idea.",["$","br","2",{}],"Overcooking foods should be avoided.",["$","br","4",{}],"Many delicious foods are high in antioxidants and should be incorporated into your regular diet. Here are some other popular foods that have naturally high antioxidant content:"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","3",{"children":["Blackberries"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","4",{"children":["Blueberries"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","5",{"children":["Strawberries"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","6",{"children":["Pomegranates"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","7",{"children":["Cranberries"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","8",{"children":["Raspberries"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","9",{"children":["Dark chocolate (low sugar)"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","10",{"children":["Artichokes (cooked)"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","11",{"children":["Spices (ex. ginger, oregano, turmeric, cumin)"],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],["$","p","12",{"children":[["$","strong","0",{"children":"GREEN"}],["$","br","1",{}],"Drinking daily green tea also increases antioxidant intake, however we do not recommend over one cup of decaffeinated green tea per day because the caffeine could interfere with fertility. Green tea is minimally processed, which maintains its healthy properties. Though the decaffeination process does reduce the antioxidant content, simply adding 50mg of liquid Vitamin C to each cup of decaffeinated green tea can significantly increase your antioxidant intake.",["$","br","3",{}],["$","br","4",{}],["$","strong","5",{"children":"CAFFEINE"}],["$","br","6",{}],"Excessive consumption of caffeinated products by the female, such as coffee, tea, colas, and chocolate may decrease fertility, although studies are conflicting. To be cautious, limit intake to a minimum. A maximum of one cup per day is advised. Caffeine is not harmful for the male partner’s fertility.","$L3","$L4","$L5","$L6","Other nutritional supplements have antioxidant properties and increase blood flow, helping to promote healthy conditions for eggs and embryos."],"style":{"textAlign":"left"}}],"$L7","$L8","$L9"]}],"$undefined"]}]}]]}],["$La","$Lb","$Lc"],"$Ld"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"05GYi4r0lZvKRQ0iy_h2K"}
